# OpenCode Client Application Documentation

## Overview

The OpenCode Client is a modern web application built with React, designed to provide an interactive chat interface for interacting with various Large Language Models (LLMs) via a backend service. At its core, any web application fundamentally involves displaying information and responding to user interactions. React, as a declarative JavaScript library, simplifies this by allowing developers to describe the desired UI state, and React handles the underlying Document Object Model (DOM) manipulations.

This document deconstructs the OpenCode Client application from its foundational architecture to its specific features and development tooling. It explores how the application initializes, manages data, handles user input, and maintains a consistent, type-safe codebase. We will reason from first principles, understanding *why* certain architectural choices and tools were made, rather than just *what* they are.

