### 2.4. Utilization of `openapi-types.ts` for Type-Safe Communication

The `src/types/openapi-types.ts` file is an auto-generated artifact from an OpenAPI (Swagger) specification. Its fundamental purpose is to serve as the single source of truth for API contract definitions, ensuring **type-safe communication** between the frontend and backend.

By generating these types, `openapi-typescript` provides compile-time checks. This means that any mismatch between the frontend's understanding of the API and the actual API contract will be caught during development, significantly reducing runtime errors and improving developer efficiency. Components and hooks import and use these types to ensure that data consumed from API calls conforms to the expected schema.

